# SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0
xtier: placement engine, plus kernel support for the baseline systems

Everything in the xtier-only patch, and additionally the kernel-side
changes needed to run the systems xTier is compared against. Apply this
one only if you want to reproduce the comparison; xTier itself needs none
of it.

  mm/memory-tiers.c   Treat node 0 as the top tier and node 1 as its
  kernel/sched/fair.c demotion target, and give node 1 a slower abstract
                      distance. On a machine emulating CXL with a second
                      NUMA node the BIOS emits no HMAT, so every node
                      defaults to the same tier and AutoNUMA tiering and
                      TPP become no-ops. Also pins the AutoNUMA scan
                      period, which otherwise oscillates during a run.

  mm/vmscan.c         A sysctl, freqtier_disable_kswapd_shrink, that stops
  kernel/sysctl.c     kswapd reclaiming from the top tier. Needed when an
                      external tiering runtime owns demotion.

  mm/htmm_*.c         The Memtis access-tracking subsystem (SOSP 2023),
  include/linux/htmm.h  ported from its 5.15 base to 6.11. Built under
  and integration     CONFIG_HTMM. Memtis is GPL-2.0; see THIRD_PARTY.md
  points              for attribution.

